  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Idaho received $3.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state saw 9,266 awards at an average award size of $379K, and obligations fell 10.8% year over year. The Department of Energy is the dominant buyer, obligating $2.5B. Remediation Services and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services are among the largest industry recipients, with $539M and $2B respectively. BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC and IDAHO ENVIRONMENTAL COALITION LLC lead vendors, with $2B and $533M in obligations. Year-by-year totals show FY26 at $3.5B following FY25 at $3.9B and FY24 at $3.8B. The spending mix highlights large energy and environmental contracts alongside substantial air transportation and construction work, reflected by multiple aviation and construction vendors in the top 10. These figures are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 federal spending in Idaho compare with recent years?",
        "body": "FY26 obligations total $3.5B. FY25 obligations were $3.9B and FY24 obligations were $3.8B. FY23 obligations were $3.2B, FY22 obligations were $2.5B, and FY21 obligations were $2.8B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors lead Idaho federal spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy obligates $2.5B, followed by the Department of Agriculture at $573M and the Department of Defense at $184M. All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounts for $2B and Remediation Services accounts for $539M. BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC has $2B in obligations and IDAHO ENVIRONMENTAL COALITION LLC has $533M."
      }
    ]
  },
